# Line endings are normalized in the repository, not in the working tree.
#
# ## Why this file exists
#
# It was added in Phase 21, and the reason is worth recording because the symptom
# is very misleading.
#
# This repository was checked out on Windows with no `core.autocrlf` set and no
# `.gitattributes` present. Git therefore stored **LF** in every blob and left
# **CRLF** in the working tree — which is fine — but on a *later* checkout the
# working tree came back CRLF while the index still compared against LF. The
# result was `git status` reporting **58 modified files and ~19,000 changed
# lines** when exactly **13 files** had been edited.
#
# 45 of those files were pure line-ending noise. A reviewer looking at that diff
# sees a rewrite of the whole test suite. Worse, a contributor running
# `git checkout .` to clean up would **discard the real edits** along with it,
# because git cannot tell the two apart.
#
# That is the property that makes this file necessary rather than tidy: without
# it, an unrelated mistake destroys uncommitted work.
#
# ## What it guarantees
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` — text files are stored with LF in the repository and
# checked out with LF on every platform, including Windows. Editors and tools
# handle display line endings themselves; the bytes on disk stay consistent,
# which is what makes a diff readable and a bisect meaningful.
#
# Binary files are declared explicitly rather than left to `text=auto`'s
# detection. Git's heuristic is right almost always, and being wrong about it
# silently corrupts a file, so the types this project can plausibly gain are
# named. Add to this list rather than relying on the guess.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never text-normalised, never line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.7z binary
*.ex5 binary
*.ex4 binary

# MQL5 sources and the parity JSON are text like any other, but named explicitly
# because Phase 21 introduces them and a reviewer should not have to reason
# about it.
*.mqh text eol=lf
*.mq5 text eol=lf
